 ## Structured resume packet
 
 `resume --run RUN --spec CURRENT_SPEC.json` reads one locked snapshot containing retained budgets, progress references, task captures, validated evidence references, native handles when retained, and PR-wide unfinished claims. Repeat `--spec` for known current tasks. Current specs use ordinary freshness checks; an omitted governing spec remains explicitly missing and never implies reusable coverage. Missing or damaged original evidence remains explicit. Read the referenced original results and progress before assessing findings or exact acceptances. The packet makes no mutations, infers no governing inputs and never authorizes recovery or publication. Reconcile unfinished native/domain work and obtain the existing recovery authority before using ordinary recovery commands.
+
+## Selective progress and original task evidence
+
+`progress --run RUN [--task TASK_KEY] [--after CURSOR] [--limit 20]` returns complete progress entries with their original positions, a scanned count, total history count and `next_cursor`. Keep the cursor even at the end to retrieve later appends. Cursors bind the PR, run, task filter and consumed history prefix; changed or truncated consumed history blocks reuse of the cursor. Page reads and task filters never establish review coverage or authorize recovery. Task filtering uses retained claim ownership, not inferred finding text. Unassociated historical entries remain available in the unfiltered full history.
+
+`task-evidence --key TASK_KEY` returns validated, complete original results and normalized findings from every retained attempt, with missing or damaged artifacts explicit. Original output remains base64 encoded with its original byte hash. Evidence access does not check freshness: supply current specs to ordinary status/start before relying on reuse. Existing compact/full status and original artifacts remain available. Use full progress when assessing complete dispositions or exact human acceptances beyond the selected page/filter.
